cogenosis, requiring specific treatments.", "NEPHROMEGALY:Nephromegaly can be associated with glucogenosis and may present with proteinuria and renal insufficiency.", "METABOLIC ACIDOSIS:Metabolic acidosis can occur in patients with glucogenosis, particularly in the context of hypoglycemia.", "GLUCOGENOSIS DE TIPO I:Glucogenosis de tipo I is a metabolic disorder characterized by the deficiency of the enzyme glucose-6-phosphatase, leading to hypoglycemia and lactic acidosis.", "ENFERMEDAD DE VON GIERKE:Enfermedad de Von Gierke is a condition marked by the deficiency of glucose-6-phosphatase, resulting in the accumulation of glycogen in the liver and associated metabolic issues.", "BIOQUÍMICO:Bioquímico refers to the biochemical analysis performed to diagnose conditions like glucogenosis de tipo I and enfermedad de Von Gierke.", "GLUCOGENOSIS MUSCULAR:Glucogenosis muscular is a category of glycogen storage diseases that primarily affect muscle tissue, resulting in muscle-related symptoms.", "GLUCOGENOSIS GENERALIZADA:Glucogenosis generalizada encompasses glycogen storage diseases that affect multiple organs and systems in the body.", "BAJA ESTATURA:Baja estatura is a clinical symptom that can occur in patients with glucogenosis, particularly in hepatic forms.", "HIPERLACTACIDEMIA:Hiperlactacidemia is a condition of elevated lactate levels in the blood, often seen in metabolic disorders like glucogenosis."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}